      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Georg Thieme Verlag Stuttgart · New York.",
        "AbstractText": "Neurenteric cysts are rare benign developmental lesions of the central nervous system which are lined by endodermal cell-derived epithelium. Here we present a 17-year-old male who presented with acute onset headache and cerebellar ataxia. He was found to have a hyperdense lesion of the cerebellar vermis on CT scan. The lesion was hyperintense on T\u2081-weighted and hypointense on T\u2082-weighted MR images. Surgical resection of the cyst revealed hemorrhage into the neurenteric cyst."
      },
